HST Office: the ribbon stays on a contextual tab while its object stays selected.

After a command on a selected picture, table, shape or chart (Picture Format, Table Design, Shape Format...),
the ribbon went back to the Home tab and the user had to click the contextual tab again; Office keeps it. A
command on the object often rebuilds the selection's shells or unmarks and marks the object again, and every
step is broadcast as a context change within the same dispatch: an SfxShell that leaves the dispatcher's stack
broadcasts the Default context (sfx2 ContextChangeBroadcaster::Deactivate), Writer's SwView::SelectShell pops
and pushes every shell when the selection type changes (a row or column selection in a table, for example),
and SdrEditView::ReplaceObjectAtView (compress, replace or filter a picture in Slides, Draw and Sheets)
unmarks the old object and marks the new one, each mark change sending a selection context. The ribbon saw
for example Graphic, Default, Frame, Graphic: the contextual tab was hidden, the ribbon fell back to the
default tab, and when the tab came back it was not selected again, because a selection context does not
open its tab (only an insert command or a double-click does).

NotebookbarTabControlBase::SetContext now remembers the contextual page that is current when a context change
starts and, when a later change of the same burst shows that page again, selects it again, unless that
change itself opened another contextual page (an insert command, a view mode). The remembered page is
forgotten by an idle task, so the decision waits for the end of the command's burst of changes instead of
a fixed delay: when the object really is deselected the default tab stays, and selecting an object later
still leaves the ribbon on the current tab. The same step keeps the shape tab when the context moves between
two contexts that both show it (Draw and DrawLine). The two decisions are plain functions in
vcl/inc/HstContextualKeepTab.hxx. LibreOfficeKit does not take this path.

